<!--Post: 8825--><!--Time: 1109361622-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8825"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 12:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please keep in mind that that sketch is the memory of a pre-teen who had just been traumatized for something like 10 hours. It may be very close, but who knows? There were two involved, possibly three. One poster on a chat board has named who they thought were resonsible. All were young men from the area. and all are now dead. BTK would seem a little old for that sketch, he would have been around 32 or more. that sketch is of a person around 24, and the facial features, to me, clearly indicate at least partial Native American heritage. I think this is a little too much of a reach.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
